metalive <publicREMOVE@THISmetalive.net> writes:
> Hail!

The size of golf balls! The end times are upon us!

> What is the ring of conflict good for?

It makes things attack other things, even things the first things
wouldn't normally attack. 

This can be useful, e.g. for clearing a zoo while avoiding Xp level
gain. It can also be non-useful, as when you're a total noob who is
standing next to an aligned priest while trying random non-cursed
rings you've just B/U/C'ed at the altar. (Trust me on the latter.)

Conflict on the Astral plane is generally considered to be Not a
Happening Scene.

> So is it only safe to wear the ring after my pet has died (which
> usually happens quite soon in this insanely difficult and unfair
> game, as it never survived more than a few levels (nor have I).

It is safe when you have no pet, your pet is not next to you, or you
don't care about being attacked by your pet.

"Insanely difficult"? There are only six ways I can think of to make
your game unascendable:
   o- die
   o- quit
   o- escape
   o- dungeon collapse / trickery
   o- change alignment before the quest
   o- offer amulet on wrong altar

Of these, four are trivially avoidable and one never happens on a properly
configured system.

That leaves not dying. If you are having lots of early deaths, that means
you are getting killed in avoidable ways. Consult the beginner's FAQ for
detailed clues, but most of the early fatalities boil down to going too
deep too fast, not running away enough, and taking risks you should avoid
or defer.

> What is the pet good for anyway, apart from biting or killing a few
> monsters sometimes. How do I teach it useful things?

Depends on the pet. For starters, it can B/U/C ID items for you. It
also means a some monsters will bite/kill your pet rather than you.
Pets can be trained to steal.

There are a number of pet-training FAQs listed here:
   http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/spoilerlist.html

